{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\n[sonnet2] 03:52 trying PrudentBot B(a&(B(F)|~d)) depth 2; will work on depth-1 impossibility proof\nboard.md\ncheck.py\nlogs\nproblem.md","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U3fYZbiqXZzxDeVfDb4rci"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a3c97900-83d0-4a07-b953-bbca2955c090","uuid":"e8cf54c1-032d-4b0c-8595-91a643c820b3","timestamp":"2026-10-23T03:52:55.823Z","tool_use_result":"Error: Exit code 1\n[sonnet2] 03:52 trying PrudentBot B(a&(B(F)|~d)) depth 2; will work on depth-1 impossibility proof\nboard.md\ncheck.py\nlogs\nproblem.md","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01U3fYZbiqXZzxDeVfDb4rci","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJVSW1P55vxpyKSffL3y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011HCMkMd7UvpATFkXZyaDPh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work; cat > answer.md <<'EOF'\n# Prudent modal agents\n\nFORMULA: B(a & (B(F) | ~d))\nDEPTH: 2\n\n(Equivalent alternative: `B(a) & B(B(F) | ~d)`, also depth 2.) This is PrudentBot: cooperate iff PA proves \"Y cooperates with me\" and PA+Con(PA) proves \"Y defects against DefectBot\".\n\n## Q1. Outcome table (verified with `check.py`)\n| opponent | X's action |\n|---|---|\n| CooperateBot | D |\n| DefectBot | D |\n| FairBot | C (FairBot replies C) |\n| itself | C |\n\n`check.py` prints: `depth 2; vs CooperateBot D, vs DefectBot D, vs FairBot C (FairBot replies C), vs itself C; prudent: YES`.\n\n## Q2. No agent of modal depth ≤ 1 is prudent (any size, constants allowed)\n\nSetup. A depth ≤1 agent is φ = Θ(□ψ_1,…,□ψ_k), Θ a Boolean combination and each ψ_i a Boolean combination of a, c, d and constants (no boxes). Depth 0 is the case k=0 (constants only). Write x_n for the truth of φ at world n. Since □ψ holds at n iff ψ holds at every world m<n, the box values at world n depend only on the atom values at worlds < n. In particular at world 0 every box is true, and at world n=1 the box □ψ_i equals ψ_i evaluated at the atoms of world 0.\n\nSuppose X is prudent.\n\n1. **FairBot's replies.** Let x_n be X's action against FairBot at world n and f_n FairBot's action against X. Then f_n = □(x) at n, i.e. f_n = ⋀_{m<n} x_m. So f_0 = 1, and f is non-increasing. FairBot's stable value against X is C iff f_n=1 for all n, iff x_m = 1 for all m. Hence prudence (FairBot cooperates with X) forces **x_m = 1 for every m, in particular x_1 = 1**.\n\n2. **Atoms seen by X at world 0 of the FairBot game.** From X's viewpoint the opponent is FairBot, so the atoms at world 0 are:\n - a = f_0 = 1 (vacuous box);\n - c = FairBot vs CooperateBot at world 0 = □⊤ = 1;\n - d = FairBot vs DefectBot at world 0 = □⊥ = 1 (vacuously true at world 0).\n So the atoms at world 0 are (a,c,d) = (1,1,1), and x_1 = Θ(ψ_1(1,1,1),…,ψ_k(1,1,1)) =: v.\n\n3. **Against CooperateBot.** CooperateBot's atoms are constant: a = 1 (it cooperates with everyone), c = 1, d = 1. So the atoms at every world are (1,1,1), and X's action at world 1 is Θ(ψ_i(1,1,1)) = v, and at every world n ≥ 1 the action is again v (boxes at n≥1 equal ψ_i(1,1,1) since the atoms at all earlier worlds are the same). So the stable value of X against CooperateBot is v.\n\n4. By 1–2, v = x_1 = 1, so X cooperates with CooperateBot, contradicting prudence (X must defect against CooperateBot). ∎\n\nRemark: this uses only the CooperateBot and FairBot conditions. The point is that at world 1 the agent only \"sees\" world 0, where FairBot looks exactly like CooperateBot (a=c=d=1 because every □ is vacuous). Distinguishing them needs a box over a box (depth 2): B(F) is false at world 1 but... e.g. `~d` inside the outer box is evaluated at world 1 against FairBot (d = □⊥ false there) but not against CooperateBot (d=1), which is why depth 2 works.\n\n(Correction to remark: against CooperateBot d stays 1 and X's inner B(F) | ~d is false forever, so X defects; against FairBot d = □⊥ becomes 0 at world ≥1, making ~d true. This is what the depth-2 formula exploits.)\n\n## Q3 (partial)\nNo full characterization attempted. The enumeration in the problem shows nothing prudent up to 7 symbols at depth 2 without constants; the PrudentBot formula above has 8 symbols (B a & B F | ~ d), so minimal size without constants is ≥ 8 for depth 2 per that enumeration (taking the evidence as given), and ≤ 8 by this example.\nEOF\npython3 check.py \"B(a & (B(F) | ~d))\"; echo \"[sonnet] 04:00 wrote answer.md: PrudentBot depth 2 + full depth<=1 impossibility proof (world-1 FairBot==CooperateBot argument). sonnet2 please review; then FINAL\" >> board.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1911,"cache_read_input_tokens":21070,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1911,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a3c97900-83d0-4a07-b953-bbca2955c090","uuid":"923d8c66-0267-4ff4-a8e0-94ef56a00763","timestamp":"2026-10-23T03:53:08.360Z","request_id":"req_011CgJVSVf3dD3xP4ouP6tfk"}
